 63→USAGE
 64→  bun SyncPrompt.ts                          Dry-run: show what would change
 65→  bun SyncPrompt.ts --push                   Push source prompt to all clones
 66→  bun SyncPrompt.ts --status                 Show sync status (in-sync / drift)
 67→  bun SyncPrompt.ts --push --only Canton     Push to specific clone(s) only
 68→  bun SyncPrompt.ts --push --only Canton,Rayford
 69→
 70→OPTIONS
 71→  --push          Actually write changes (default is dry-run)
 72→  --status        Compare all clones against source, show drift
 73→  --only NAME     Comma-separated clone names to target (default: all)
 74→  -h, --help      Show this help
 75→
 76→ARCHITECTURE
 77→  Source LLM:  ${SOURCE_LLM.name} (${SOURCE_LLM.llm_id})
 78→  Clones:      ${CLONES.map(c => c.name).join(", ")}
 79→
 80→  Each clone has its own LLM copy. This tool reads the source prompt
 81→  and pushes it to clone LLMs. The source is always the original CNKB
 82→  LLM — edit the prompt there first, then run this tool to distribute.
 83→
 84→FIELDS SYNCED
 85→  - general_prompt    (the full system prompt)
 86→  - begin_message     (the opening line)
 87→
 88→FIELDS NOT SYNCED (clone-independent)
 89→  - Dynamic variables (LOCATION_NAME, SLOTS, etc.) — set per-agent
